{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Landed as TWO changes, in that order, because one would not work.\n\n2320 (merged first): declare REBAR_MUTATION_ALLOW_UNSANDBOXED on the mutation gate step and correct its stale 'fails CLOSED' comment. A no-op at the time — ambient CI still waived implicitly — which is exactly why it was safe to land first.\n\n2321 (merged second): delete the CI-keyed fail-open branch and its sole-purpose _ci_environment helper, invert the tests, and drop the CI-fallback prose from docs/local-dev-env.md. Net -19 lines in the source: the fix is subtractive, leaving ONE named waiver instead of adding a second knob.\n\nWhy the order was forced, learned the hard way: my first attempt (2319, abandoned) did both in one commit and the mutation gate ABORTED. The Verified lane takes the workflow DEFINITION from trusted main and the TREE from the change, so my code change took effect while my workflow declaration did not — the gate had neither a sandbox nor a waiver. That is the same definition-vs-tree skew documented for 0d22, biting in the opposite direction.\n\nRED proofs by real mutation: reinstating an ambient-CI waiver failed 5 tests; removing the named opt-out failed 2. Broad suite 15384 passed, 0 failed. CI green on 2321 with no failures.\n\nResidual, stated plainly: the mutation gate still runs UNSANDBOXED on its lane — that exposure is unchanged by this ticket. What changed is that it is now DECLARED in a reviewed file rather than inherited from an ambient variable, and a workstation with CI=1 exported no longer gets the same silent waiver. Giving that lane a real sandbox, as 0d22 did for the enforcement lane, remains the better end state."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787914913581838001,"uuid":"5c7424c5-d6ca-4d74-95ff-059575463bed"}